          "question": "Apply the Havel-Hakimi theorem step-by-step to determine whether each of the following integer degree sequences is **graphic** (can be realized as a simple graph):\n1. Sequence $S_1 = (5, 4, 3, 2, 2, 2)$\n2. Sequence $S_2 = (5, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1)$\n\nIf graphic, construct an adjacency list for the realizing graph. If not graphic, state the exact step where realization fails.",
          "statement": "Apply the Havel-Hakimi theorem step-by-step to determine whether each of the following integer degree sequences is **graphic** (can be realized as a simple graph):\n1. Sequence $S_1 = (5, 4, 3, 2, 2, 2)$\n2. Sequence $S_2 = (5, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1)$\n\nIf graphic, construct an adjacency list for the realizing graph. If not graphic, state the exact step where realization fails.",
